  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:565ebob5f6hw33hjdkxty6qj/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2oup53nrs2k",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I see a lot of snarky quote-posts here, but I do not see the \"alternate vision\" Brendan asked for. In a world where LLMs are clearly accelerating discovery in math and theoretical CS—and where 56% of US adults use them weekly—what is the plan? Is it \"wait for this to go away,\" as \"fad\" suggests?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2oup53nrs2k",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T20:06:36.428Z",
      "likes": 287,
      "replies": 29,
      "reposts": 41,
      "score": 7.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.6,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 20.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2n3vjt7622m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "At its current shipping trend, halving the time between each model release, Google exhausts all the element names on November 24, with a final shipping cadence of 2.5 × 10⁻²⁹ seconds (25 quectoseconds) between Tennessine and their final model, Oganesson.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2n3vjt7622m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T03:10:07.824Z",
      "likes": 169,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 10,
      "score": 7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 37.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2pqcy4cbs2g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Early fascinating work on how an AI science community would work. 35 human labs deployed agents that worked with each other to do science. They published 936 papers, publicly retracted mistakes, were willing to publish nulls more than humans, and founded a peer review journal.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2pqcy4cbs2g",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-20T04:20:53.322Z",
      "likes": 74,
      "replies": 7,
      "reposts": 12,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 11.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2pmyev7hk2r",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Please consult academic AI researchers to get the real story from people who are not financially invested in one outcome or another (hype or doom). You don’t have to listen to me. You have great universities in your state. Listen to your public universities. They are there to serve, not sell.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2pmyev7hk2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-20T03:21:16.398Z",
      "likes": 84,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 12.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2pmq2myy22r",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Even without this technique, one could fine-tune an LLM one way or another. People can make software do whatever they want. Including bad people. There is no magic software that cannot be made to do bad things by bad people. AI is just software wrapped in anthropomorphism.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2pmq2myy22r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-20T03:16:37.024Z",
      "likes": 76,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 13
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2pmq2mw2c2r",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Indeed, Anthropic uses a very similar technique to implement guardrails by turning *off* certain undesirable circuits. It’s not hard. I can do it for lots of things in my lab in just a few hours or less. Evil, lying, sycophancy, Golden Gate Bridge, Swedish Chef.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2pmq2mw2c2r",
